<p style="
             font-size: 16px;
             color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
             line-height: 1.5;
             margin-top: 1.2em;
             margin-bottom: 2em;
             word-wrap: break-word;
         ">Output example:</p><img src="https://public-hunt-static-blog-assets.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/2-2026/Hunting+OpenClaw+Exposures+CVE-2026-25253+in+Internet-Facing+AI+Agent+Gateways+-+figure+12.png" alt="Figure 12: Redacted Header Hash (SHA256) with Port Filter - 7,130 Results" title class="markdown-image" data-src="https://public-hunt-static-blog-assets.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/2-2026/Hunting+OpenClaw+Exposures+CVE-2026-25253+in+Internet-Facing+AI+Agent+Gateways+-+figure+12.png" data-alt="Figure 12: Redacted Header Hash (SHA256) with Port Filter - 7,130 Results" style="
                display: block;
                margin: 1em auto -1em auto;
                max-width: 85%;
                max-height: 600px;
                cursor: zoom-in;
                overflow: hidden;
                border-radius: 6px;
                box-shadow: -1px 4px 23px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);"><span class="figure" style="
                font-size: 14px;
                color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
                font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
                line-height: 1.5;
                margin-top: 1.2em;
                text-align: center;
                font-weight: 400;
                margin-bottom: 2em;
                display: block;
                font-style: italic;
                margin-inline: auto;
                max-width: 80%;
            ">Figure 12: Redacted Header Hash (SHA256) with Port Filter - 7,130 Results</span><h3 style="font-size: 24px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 1.2em;">Detection Strategy 4: HTML Body Hashing</h3><p style="
             font-size: 16px;
             color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
             line-height: 1.5;
             margin-top: 1.2em;
             margin-bottom: 2em;
             word-wrap: break-word;
         ">The OpenClaw web interface produces consistent HTML output because it is built using Vite with a React frontend that generates deterministic builds. By computing hashes of the HTML response body, we can create stable fingerprints that identify instances regardless of the HTTP headers they return. This approach is particularly effective for detecting instances running behind reverse proxies or load balancers that may modify header values.</p><p style="
             font-size: 16px;
             color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
             line-height: 1.5;
             margin-top: 1.2em;
             margin-bottom: 2em;
             word-wrap: break-word;
         ">We employed three complementary hash algorithms for body fingerprinting. SHA256 provides cryptographically strong exact matching for unmodified deployments. Murmur3 offers faster computation for large-scale scanning operations. TLSH (Trend Micro Locality Sensitive Hash) enables fuzzy matching that can detect modified versions of the framework with minor HTML changes, making it invaluable for finding customized or obfuscated deployments.</p><p style="
             font-size: 16px;
             color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
             line-height: 1.5;
             margin-top: 1.2em;
             margin-bottom: 2em;
             word-wrap: break-word;
         ">The body hashing approach identified approximately 6,800 instances across all three algorithms. The slight variation in results between hash types reflects differences in how each algorithm handles whitespace and encoding variations. TLSH is particularly valuable for detecting instances where operators have made cosmetic modifications to the interface.</p><p style="
             font-size: 16px;
             color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
             line-height: 1.5;
             margin-top: 1.2em;
             margin-bottom: 2em;
             word-wrap: break-word;
         ">The following query uses exact SHA256 hashes of the HTML body to identify unmodified OpenClaw deployments.</p><p style="
             font-size: 16px;
             color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
             line-height: 1.5;
             margin-top: 1.2em;
             margin-bottom: 2em;
             word-wrap: break-word;
         "><strong>Query (SHA256 Body Hash):</strong></p><pre><code class="language-sql"><code class=" language-sql" data-raw="SELECT ip, port, hostname, html.head.title
FROM httpv2
WHERE html.body.hash.sha256 IN (
    'DECF58D16C7436B434ED551703F510564AA5E17C19E9CAC5220E0A257DC5D55D',
    '796A9FC9101556A326DBD2B18790EDD6FAF20A38FBFE260C855FDE9560801661',
    '995880C9E738FFE27183671D515FBA80DDB14DDBACE728E91568499B95724CDF',
    '57B7EDD7DDB95F9DC4C4CC6F1976BCEA781AE134B10E013B9EBC390007C3A5F6',
    '9A2EB53F0F3526ED528B342C8300C0BD25312F23B1F22471617E6FEBC32E0B83',
    'F9BCCE51878B4B206F4F9B878F0A93E022E0E3C5C1739851FFA1ED474C865575',
    'E0726B08D60A26BC0CCC3B935959D53655B008619B2B28BC4D0163C8791E415E'
)
AND port IN (18789, 18791)
"><span class="hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> ip, port, hostname, html.head.title
<span class="hljs-keyword">FROM</span> httpv2
<span class="hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> html.body.hash.sha256 <span class="hljs-keyword">IN</span> (
    <span class="hljs-string">'DECF58D16C7436B434ED551703F510564AA5E17C19E9CAC5220E0A257DC5D55D'</span>,
    <span class="hljs-string">'796A9FC9101556A326DBD2B18790EDD6FAF20A38FBFE260C855FDE9560801661'</span>,
    <span class="hljs-string">'995880C9E738FFE27183671D515FBA80DDB14DDBACE728E91568499B95724CDF'</span>,
    <span class="hljs-string">'57B7EDD7DDB95F9DC4C4CC6F1976BCEA781AE134B10E013B9EBC390007C3A5F6'</span>,
    <span class="hljs-string">'9A2EB53F0F3526ED528B342C8300C0BD25312F23B1F22471617E6FEBC32E0B83'</span>,
    <span class="hljs-string">'F9BCCE51878B4B206F4F9B878F0A93E022E0E3C5C1739851FFA1ED474C865575'</span>,
    <span class="hljs-string">'E0726B08D60A26BC0CCC3B935959D53655B008619B2B28BC4D0163C8791E415E'</span>
)
<span class="hljs-keyword">AND</span> port <span class="hljs-keyword">IN</span> (<span class="hljs-number">18789</span>, <span class="hljs-number">18791</span>)
</code>
                <div class="code-actions"><div class="copy-trigger" style="width: 80px;
